#X obj 631 8 conv.color2rgba;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 206 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object converts a color given as a name or a hex
value into separate R \, G \, B and A channel values. By default the
output values are integers in the range [0 \, 255]. With the @float
flag \, the output values are in the range [0 \, 1] instead. By default
the channel values are sent to four separate outlets. If the @pack
flag is set \, all four values are packed into a single list sent to
the first outlet.;
#X text 240 214 Supported named colors: black \, blue \, cyan \, gold
\, gray \, green \, lime \, magenta \, navy \, olive \, orange \, pink
\, purple \, red \, white \, yellow.;
